# cuttle stealth-chromium patch #52 - persona speechSynthesis voice list.
#
# Source: chromium 151.0.7922.137
#   third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis.cc
#   third_party/blink/renderer/modules/speech/speech_synthesis.h
#
# Authored for cuttle, not derived from the clark series - hence the Cuttle*
# symbol names. It references clark::switches only because the shared
# fingerprint-switch header the whole series uses lives in that namespace.
#
# The container has no speech-dispatcher, and Chromium only registers the Google
# network-voice component extension under BUILDFLAG(GOOGLE_CHROME_BRANDING), so
# getVoices() answers [] on every Chromium-based build while the persona claims
# desktop Chrome.
#
# Every value is transcribed from real Chrome 151 captures - macOS: 199 voices
# (180 local + 19 network); Windows 11: 22 (3 local + the same 19, identical set
# and order). voiceURI equals name on both.
#
# Three measured behaviours are reproduced deliberately:
#   1. The first synchronous getVoices() returns [] on both platforms; the list
#      only appears on voiceschanged. Hooking OnSetVoiceList rather than
#      getVoices() preserves that - a synchronously populated list is a tell.
#   2. macOS dispatches once with everything. Windows dispatches twice: the
#      network voices first, then again once SAPI has enumerated its locals,
#      which sort ahead of them.
#   3. Exactly one voice is flagged default and it is always the CURRENT list's
#      first entry. During the Windows intermediate stage that is a network
#      voice ("Google Deutsch"), not a local one - so the flag is derived at
#      publish time rather than pinned to a name in the tables.
#
# The list does NOT track the persona locale: real Chrome with its locale
# overridden to de-DE still reports Samantha/en-US on macOS and Microsoft
# David/en-US on Windows. A locale-matched default would be less realistic.
#
# Gated on fingerprint mode; --fingerprint-voices=false opts out.
